> At 08:28 AM 10/9/02 -0400, Paul Kraus wrote:
> >What mailing list or web page do I want to check regularly for security
> >updates and kernel updates? Is there a way I can be notified without
> >having to check?

Maybe you're less newbie than me and already know this, but I'll try 
and give a piece of important advice in the way of kernel updating just 
in case. Advice follows: be sure to make a backup of your current working 
kernel before trying to recompile or compile a new one. Name it 
"vmlinuz-2.4.x-x_backup" or something like that. Then, if your recompile 
or new compile is less than successful, you can boot to one you know works 
ok on your system. Doing that could have saved me some headaches in the 
past.

